00:01:33.520 --> 00:01:38.960
When Flight 807, a large-scale space bus, landed
on Planet Duke, the cabin was completely empty.

00:01:38.960 --> 00:01:42.230
All 463 passengers and crew
members had vanished.

00:01:42.230 --> 00:01:44.130
Was it a paranormal phenomenon or a mystery?

00:01:44.130 --> 00:01:48.340
Then, we received a ransom note from someone
claiming to have kidnapped the 463 people.

00:01:48.340 --> 00:01:53.080
What's more, accident investigator Eddie's
daughter Melody was one of the passengers!

00:01:53.080 --> 00:01:55.940
Right. I feel so sorry
for her big brother, Arthur.

00:01:55.940 --> 00:01:59.040
However, Arthur was attacked
by an unknown assailant.

00:01:59.180 --> 00:02:03.320
Yuri believes that Arthur holds
the key to solving this case.

00:02:03.320 --> 00:02:05.720
And then, we received
a second ransom note.

00:02:05.720 --> 00:02:09.760
The kidnappers increased the ransom tenfold,
and demanded something called "File-E."

00:02:09.760 --> 00:02:12.190
What is File-E?

00:02:12.190 --> 00:02:18.160
We Did It!
463 People Found!

00:02:24.670 --> 00:02:25.610
File-E...

00:02:27.810 --> 00:02:30.610
The kidnappers raised the ransom tenfold.

00:02:30.610 --> 00:02:33.380
And they also want something called File-E.

00:02:33.380 --> 00:02:35.910
What do you suppose File-E is?

00:02:37.020 --> 00:02:38.820
I'll take care of that.

00:02:39.990 --> 00:02:44.290
No, Papa! They're not the real
culprits! It's a lie! They're lying!

00:02:44.960 --> 00:02:48.260
No. If they're bringing up File-E,
then they have to be the kidnappers.

00:02:48.260 --> 00:02:51.230
No, they're not! They're really not!

00:02:51.230 --> 00:02:53.130
You have to believe me!

00:02:55.970 --> 00:02:56.940
Mama!

00:02:58.340 --> 00:03:00.640
I heard you got a new ransom note.

00:03:00.910 --> 00:03:03.900
No, it's not from the kidnappers!

00:03:04.150 --> 00:03:07.280
Arthur, what are you talking about?

00:03:07.280 --> 00:03:09.350
Come on, Arthur. Tell us what you know.

00:03:09.350 --> 00:03:12.080
Yeah! You'll feel a lot better
after you tell us everything.

00:03:14.060 --> 00:03:15.320
It was me.

00:03:16.020 --> 00:03:17.260
I did it...

00:03:17.260 --> 00:03:18.730
Th-That's nonsense!

00:03:18.730 --> 00:03:22.420
Impossible. No child could
pull off something like this.

00:03:23.100 --> 00:03:25.660
Papa, Mama... You're getting a divorce, right?

00:03:29.370 --> 00:03:31.670
I heard you talking about it on the phone.

00:03:31.670 --> 00:03:34.610
Melody and I won't be brother
and sister anymore, right?

00:03:34.910 --> 00:03:39.810
I thought maybe if Melody got kidnapped,
you two would work together and...

00:03:40.050 --> 00:03:41.150
Arthur...

00:03:41.150 --> 00:03:42.910
That's why you did this?

00:03:46.120 --> 00:03:47.650
The kidnapping...

00:03:48.060 --> 00:03:49.790
It never happened.

00:03:49.890 --> 00:03:51.860
The kidnapping never happened?

00:03:52.130 --> 00:03:58.560
The passengers on Flight 807 are on Flight 808.
It'll land soon, so there's no need to worry.

00:03:59.070 --> 00:04:01.870
Flight 808's destination is Ocean Rib.

00:04:04.970 --> 00:04:08.030
Jeez, could he be any more level-headed?

00:04:09.410 --> 00:04:13.370
Arthur, can you explain it in detail,
so we can all understand?

00:04:13.750 --> 00:04:18.590
I swapped the passenger lists for
Flight 807 and Flight 808 on my computer.

00:04:18.590 --> 00:04:21.220
So you did do it by computer, after all.

00:04:21.220 --> 00:04:25.390
I used to go to the SWA
computer room sometimes, to play.

00:04:26.800 --> 00:04:31.660
That's how I memorized the password rotation,
from hanging out in the computer room.

00:04:36.540 --> 00:04:41.170
When I tried logging in
from my computer, it worked.

00:04:41.540 --> 00:04:45.080
I booked the seats on
Flight 808 using fake names.

00:04:45.080 --> 00:04:49.680
Then I canceled them all right before the ship left,
and switched them with the passengers from 807.

00:04:49.680 --> 00:04:55.420
A ship can fly on autopilot, so Flight 807
flew without anyone onboard.

00:04:56.530 --> 00:04:59.430
See? There was no one
onboard from the start.

00:04:59.430 --> 00:05:03.100
That was just a lucky guess.
You had nothing to back it up.

00:05:03.100 --> 00:05:04.970
It-It was intuition. Female intuition.

00:05:04.970 --> 00:05:05.660
You little...

00:05:07.440 --> 00:05:12.270
But Arthur, what about the weight record
that showed it was a full flight?

00:05:12.470 --> 00:05:15.240
Flight 808 is the one that's full.

00:05:15.240 --> 00:05:20.840
I programmed it so all of Flight 807 and 808's
transmissions and records would switch.

00:05:21.120 --> 00:05:22.350
I see.

00:05:22.350 --> 00:05:25.220
But wait, there's one thing
that still doesn't make sense.

00:05:25.220 --> 00:05:27.290
The transmission between the
captain and the control tower...

00:05:27.290 --> 00:05:31.360
Right, the captain said
"Flight 807" in his transmission.

00:05:31.360 --> 00:05:33.830
I asked Captain Crocker to say that.

00:05:33.830 --> 00:05:35.260
You asked Captain Crocker?

00:05:35.260 --> 00:05:39.100
He always plays with me. When I
asked him, he didn't seem to mind.

00:05:39.100 --> 00:05:45.010
I figured it wouldn't be a problem, as long as I
switched the data back before Flight 808 landed.

00:05:45.010 --> 00:05:47.070
Flight 808 is missing.

00:05:47.410 --> 00:05:52.510
I just contacted Ocean Rib,
and they can't reach Flight 808.

00:06:04.690 --> 00:06:05.860
What's going on?

00:06:05.860 --> 00:06:09.500
Flight 808 is well past
its scheduled arrival time.

00:06:09.500 --> 00:06:11.560
It's no use. The ship's
not showing up on the radar.

00:06:11.870 --> 00:06:16.640
Eddie, you know who took advantage
of Arthur's hoax, don't you?

00:06:16.640 --> 00:06:19.400
The clue is File-E, isn't it?

00:06:20.380 --> 00:06:22.380
Eddie, please tell us!

00:06:22.380 --> 00:06:25.010
It's wrong to keep us in the dark
by investigating this alone!

00:06:26.820 --> 00:06:31.750
Six months ago, I was in charge of an investigation
team that uncovered a smuggling ring.

00:06:31.750 --> 00:06:34.620
At that time, we seized some important
evidence concerning the smugglers.

00:06:34.860 --> 00:06:36.660
That evidence is File-E.

00:06:36.660 --> 00:06:38.530
What is the evidence?

00:06:38.530 --> 00:06:42.220
It's their registered retinal patterns.

00:06:42.600 --> 00:06:45.530
Retinal patterns are as
good as fingerprints, right?

00:06:45.900 --> 00:06:48.730
So the kidnappers are the
remnants of that smuggling gang?

00:06:48.870 --> 00:06:49.770
Most likely.

00:06:49.770 --> 00:06:50.070
Why didn't you tell us this before?
Most likely.

00:06:50.070 --> 00:06:51.940
Why didn't you tell us this before?

00:06:51.940 --> 00:06:57.210
Some members of the ASW are
involved with the smuggling gang.

00:06:59.350 --> 00:07:01.320
I see... So that's why.

00:07:01.320 --> 00:07:04.880
You were so secretive because you were
in the middle of an undercover investigation.

00:07:05.050 --> 00:07:08.020
I'm sorry. But I know who they are now.

00:07:08.020 --> 00:07:10.120
If they're involved with
this incident, that means...

00:07:14.200 --> 00:07:16.930
It's Captain Crocker and his co-pilot Stablos.

00:07:19.730 --> 00:07:21.530
I have no doubt it's them.

00:07:28.240 --> 00:07:29.230
Arthur!

00:07:31.310 --> 00:07:34.040
He blames himself.

00:07:34.880 --> 00:07:36.610
Wait! Let Yuri handle it.

00:07:36.790 --> 00:07:38.090
I can't do that!

00:07:38.090 --> 00:07:41.540
Instead, you need to think about
why this happened in the first place.

00:07:44.490 --> 00:07:49.160
I did think, long and hard,
before we decided to file for divorce.

00:07:50.400 --> 00:07:54.340
That's why I didn't want to see Arthur.
I knew I would second-guess myself.

00:07:54.340 --> 00:07:54.570
In the end,
That's why I didn't want to see Arthur.
I knew I would second-guess myself.

00:07:54.570 --> 00:07:55.730
In the end,

00:07:57.210 --> 00:07:59.330
we have no choice but
to make a deal with them.

00:07:59.470 --> 00:08:02.500
I'll ready the 46,300,00 credits.

00:08:10.090 --> 00:08:13.210
Right then, let's look for Flight 808!

00:08:14.290 --> 00:08:18.530
They couldn't have hid a
huge ship like that so easily.

00:08:18.530 --> 00:08:19.580
You're right.

00:08:27.140 --> 00:08:28.570
You're horrible.

00:08:28.570 --> 00:08:30.330
You're horrible, Captain Crocker!

00:08:30.540 --> 00:08:32.370
I can't believe you tricked me!

00:08:32.370 --> 00:08:33.360
Arthur...

00:08:34.940 --> 00:08:36.670
I knew I'd find you here.

00:08:36.810 --> 00:08:38.480
Don't distract me.

00:08:38.480 --> 00:08:40.850
I'm going to find those guys.

00:08:41.020 --> 00:08:42.710
Oh? How?

00:08:44.350 --> 00:08:46.480
C'mon, tell me how.

00:08:48.160 --> 00:08:52.290
Remember how they sent the
ransom notes through the computer?

00:08:52.290 --> 00:08:56.230
They could do that because they knew
the password for the ASW computers.

00:08:56.230 --> 00:08:57.130
I see.

00:08:57.130 --> 00:09:02.300
So if I can figure out the password for Flight 808,
I should be able to find their current location.

00:09:02.300 --> 00:09:04.810
I see, so that's what
you're trying to do now.

00:09:04.810 --> 00:09:05.500
Yeah.

00:09:05.870 --> 00:09:11.380
But there are a bunch of different combinations,
so I have to try them all one by one.

00:09:11.380 --> 00:09:13.240
Right. Do your best, then!

00:09:16.250 --> 00:09:19.620
That's the situation on our end,
so don't worry about us.

00:09:19.620 --> 00:09:20.350
Roger.

00:09:50.650 --> 00:09:55.020
I see. No one would even notice
if someone hid a spaceship here.

00:09:55.020 --> 00:09:58.980
Yeah. Usually the management in
places like this is kinda sloppy.

00:09:59.830 --> 00:10:00.390
Huh?

00:10:06.030 --> 00:10:12.170
As you can see, this scrap yard is
equipped with 175 separate heat sensors.

00:10:12.170 --> 00:10:14.000
I-I see...

00:10:14.080 --> 00:10:18.680
That means no intruder, not even
a single rat, goes unnoticed.

00:10:18.680 --> 00:10:24.740
Therefore, if there were 463 people in the yard,
there's no way these sensors would miss them!

00:10:25.090 --> 00:10:27.990
W-What an impressive security system!

00:10:28.660 --> 00:10:30.760
Assuming they're still alive, of course.

00:10:30.760 --> 00:10:31.820
Huh?
Huh?

00:11:02.590 --> 00:11:03.490
Eddie?

00:11:06.790 --> 00:11:07.850
What's the matter?

00:11:07.960 --> 00:11:09.930
There seems to have been
a new transmission.

00:11:11.630 --> 00:11:15.130
I knew it. The kidnappers
sent new instructions!

00:11:16.300 --> 00:11:19.210
"Take ASW 011..."

00:11:19.210 --> 00:11:21.800
"...and set your radio frequency to 461."

00:11:25.110 --> 00:11:27.410
Sorry, but this is something I have to do.

00:11:28.050 --> 00:11:29.620
How about north of Area 6?

00:11:29.620 --> 00:11:32.850
There's a bad geomagnetic storm
in that area, so the radar is useless.

00:11:33.050 --> 00:11:33.720
Chief.

00:11:33.720 --> 00:11:36.660
Why, Shannon. What brings you here?

00:11:36.660 --> 00:11:40.660
There was a spacecraft that
left here about thirty minutes ago.

00:11:40.660 --> 00:11:43.130
Can you confirm its
current position on the radar?

00:11:43.130 --> 00:11:45.530
Thirty minutes ago? I'm afraid not.

00:11:45.530 --> 00:11:49.170
The radar is useless right now thanks to
all the geomagnetic storms nearby.

00:11:49.170 --> 00:11:51.300
Jeez, what a selfish husband.

00:11:53.040 --> 00:11:56.010
Eddie, you're always like this.

00:11:56.010 --> 00:11:58.310
You never tell me anything.

00:12:02.950 --> 00:12:04.540
This one's not it either.

00:12:08.660 --> 00:12:09.860
How are things going?

00:12:09.860 --> 00:12:11.020
Well...

00:12:11.660 --> 00:12:14.630
Oh, right. I brought you a friend.

00:12:15.530 --> 00:12:17.190
Calm down.

00:12:21.000 --> 00:12:22.300
Don't be such a baby.

00:12:22.670 --> 00:12:24.540
It's name is Nanmo.

00:12:24.640 --> 00:12:26.940
It's here to help you. Come on.

00:12:29.680 --> 00:12:30.970
Yuri, come in.

00:12:31.250 --> 00:12:31.810
Kei?

00:12:31.810 --> 00:12:33.300
Eddie's gone missing.

00:12:34.420 --> 00:12:37.380
The kidnappers sent new instructions,
and Eddie apparently went off by himself.

00:12:37.890 --> 00:12:39.090
You've got to be kidding!

00:12:39.090 --> 00:12:41.160
At any rate, we're going to go look for him.

00:12:41.160 --> 00:12:43.090
Do what you can to
figure out that password!

00:12:49.560 --> 00:12:50.690
Arthur...

00:12:51.630 --> 00:12:54.690
Eddie Ross. You'd better have
everything we asked for.

00:12:55.070 --> 00:12:56.870
I have the ransom money.

00:12:56.940 --> 00:12:58.040
And File-E?

00:12:58.040 --> 00:12:59.970
I have that, too. Where do you want me to go?

00:12:59.970 --> 00:13:01.670
Don't be so hasty.

00:13:22.200 --> 00:13:27.100
The landing spot is E302 W51, Point A-

00:13:28.340 --> 00:13:30.670
Dammit, where is it?

00:13:39.680 --> 00:13:40.680
Yes!

00:13:40.680 --> 00:13:42.010
Just one more number to go!

00:13:48.620 --> 00:13:53.320
Take this car and come to the
scrap yard north of the warp terminal.

00:13:56.830 --> 00:13:58.800
We did it, we did it!

00:13:58.800 --> 00:14:00.570
We figured out the password!

00:14:00.570 --> 00:14:01.740
We did it!

00:14:01.740 --> 00:14:02.040
Yeah! That's great, Arthur!
We did it!

00:14:02.040 --> 00:14:03.270
Yeah! That's great, Arthur!

00:14:03.270 --> 00:14:03.500
Yeah! That's great, Arthur!
Yeah, now we can find out where they are!

00:14:03.500 --> 00:14:06.130
Yeah, now we can find out where they are!

00:14:09.240 --> 00:14:11.580
Kei, we finally figured out the password!

00:14:13.410 --> 00:14:17.620
Flight 808 is in an underground
scrap yard north of the warp terminal.

00:14:17.620 --> 00:14:19.520
Eh? We already looked there.

00:14:19.520 --> 00:14:23.320
We're positive! The kidnappers sent their
transmissions using that scrap yard's computer.

00:14:23.320 --> 00:14:24.480
Are you sure?

00:14:24.660 --> 00:14:26.820
Kei, we'll know for sure once we get there.

00:14:28.630 --> 00:14:30.500
We'll keep looking for Eddie.

00:14:30.500 --> 00:14:32.630
You guys look for Flight 808.

00:14:32.630 --> 00:14:33.360
Okay.

00:14:40.740 --> 00:14:41.830
Crocker...

00:14:42.180 --> 00:14:44.650
Let's cut to the chase. Hand over the goods.

00:14:44.650 --> 00:14:49.420
I can't give this to you until I know
that the passengers are safe.

00:14:49.420 --> 00:14:52.010
Open the trunk and
show us what's inside first.

00:14:54.920 --> 00:14:55.650
Yo!

00:14:55.920 --> 00:14:56.990
Stablos...

00:14:56.990 --> 00:15:02.020
Life is precious, but I'll gladly take
that trunk off your dead body if I have to.

00:15:02.500 --> 00:15:04.760
Put the trunk on the lift. Move it!

00:15:12.170 --> 00:15:13.810
That's Eddie's spaceship.

00:15:13.810 --> 00:15:16.000
Looks like Arthur was right.

00:15:22.320 --> 00:15:23.980
It's definitely File-E.

00:15:24.990 --> 00:15:28.050
I had to lay low for a
long time thanks to this file.

00:15:28.360 --> 00:15:29.880
But that's all over now.

00:15:44.270 --> 00:15:47.140
Fine. Now tell me where the passengers are!

00:15:48.080 --> 00:15:49.140
Get real.

00:15:49.140 --> 00:15:50.510
So you were never going to!

00:15:57.590 --> 00:15:58.880
Farewell.

00:16:05.630 --> 00:16:06.390
Shannon!

00:16:10.470 --> 00:16:12.090
You're way more reckless than us!

00:16:16.200 --> 00:16:18.440
Jeez, you guys are persistent.

00:16:18.440 --> 00:16:21.600
You're not going to find anyone,
no matter how hard you look.

00:16:21.680 --> 00:16:25.110
He tracked this place down on his computer,
so there's no doubt that they're here.

00:16:25.250 --> 00:16:27.410
That kid doesn't know
what he's talking about.

00:16:36.260 --> 00:16:37.380
Darling!

00:16:37.490 --> 00:16:38.730
You're so reckless...

00:16:38.730 --> 00:16:38.890
You're the one who's reckless, coming here alone.
You're so reckless...

00:16:38.890 --> 00:16:42.160
You're the one who's reckless, coming here alone.

00:16:42.160 --> 00:16:44.400
We know where Flight 808 is.

00:16:44.400 --> 00:16:46.170
It's in the underground scrap yard.

00:16:46.170 --> 00:16:46.870
I see...

00:16:46.870 --> 00:16:47.240
Darling!
I see...

00:16:47.240 --> 00:16:47.670
Darling!

00:16:48.270 --> 00:16:52.830
That was quite a flashy entrance,
wasn't it, Mrs. Ross?

00:16:55.280 --> 00:16:59.050
Hey now, drop your gun.
Don't forget we have hostages.

00:16:59.050 --> 00:17:01.170
You too, lady. Put down your gun.

00:17:04.120 --> 00:17:07.280
That's right. Women should be more compliant.

00:17:07.390 --> 00:17:11.060
Try anything strange and I'll
detonate the bomb on Flight 808.

00:17:11.060 --> 00:17:13.490
Ehh? A bomb?

00:17:13.490 --> 00:17:16.790
There's a bomb on Flight 808?

00:17:17.770 --> 00:17:20.800
All 463 people will die if I press this button.

00:17:20.800 --> 00:17:23.830
No way! You can detonate it remotely?

00:17:24.170 --> 00:17:26.510
Arthur, we have another problem.

00:17:26.510 --> 00:17:29.600
There's a bomb on Flight 808.

00:17:31.050 --> 00:17:33.150
You know it's the end
of the line for you, right?

00:17:33.150 --> 00:17:37.680
Well then, I hate to see you all go,
but it's time to say goodbye.

00:17:37.750 --> 00:17:38.620
Wait!

00:17:39.020 --> 00:17:43.460
I want to look pretty if I'm going to die.
Let me at least put on some makeup, okay?

00:17:53.470 --> 00:17:58.310
I never thought my life would be
cut short in such a dirty scrap yard.

00:17:58.310 --> 00:18:01.100
I wish I could have died someplace better.

00:18:05.380 --> 00:18:07.310
Come on, Yuri. Hurry!

00:18:09.120 --> 00:18:10.050
Yuri!

00:18:13.120 --> 00:18:14.920
This! This is it!

00:18:14.920 --> 00:18:16.820
It's the spaceship for Flight 808!

00:18:16.960 --> 00:18:18.050
This?

00:18:28.800 --> 00:18:30.900
Hey, wrap it up already.

00:18:31.840 --> 00:18:34.140
It's not gonna make any difference.

00:18:34.140 --> 00:18:38.170
Jeez, can't you give a lady who's
about to die a few kind words?

00:18:39.010 --> 00:18:40.740
Just hurry it up!

00:18:41.020 --> 00:18:44.450
The least you can do is give me enough time
to put on my makeup for when I'm dead.

00:18:44.450 --> 00:18:46.610
If you don't, I might just
come back and haunt you.

00:18:49.360 --> 00:18:52.160
It's over. My partner diffused the bomb.

00:18:52.160 --> 00:18:52.490
W-What?!
It's over. My partner diffused the bomb.

00:18:52.490 --> 00:18:53.360
W-What?!

00:18:54.630 --> 00:18:55.250
Damn it!

00:19:04.310 --> 00:19:05.170
Owww...

00:19:05.170 --> 00:19:06.640
What took you so long?!

00:19:06.640 --> 00:19:09.380
Now I'm caked in makeup,
just like you always are!

00:19:09.380 --> 00:19:11.980
Hmph. At least you're not
such an eyesore now.

00:19:11.980 --> 00:19:13.180
Why you!

00:19:13.180 --> 00:19:15.680
Listen, both of you. Don't kill them.

00:19:15.680 --> 00:19:17.310
They're important witnesses.

00:19:17.390 --> 00:19:18.680
Aye-aye, sir!
Aye-aye, sir!

00:19:19.250 --> 00:19:20.740
Get off of me!

00:19:22.920 --> 00:19:24.980
Crocker! Where are you?

00:19:25.130 --> 00:19:27.290
Come out, and we'll go easy on you.

00:19:35.470 --> 00:19:36.440
What the?

00:19:38.270 --> 00:19:39.470
N-No way!

00:19:47.050 --> 00:19:48.350
K-Kei!

00:19:48.820 --> 00:19:50.080
I'll squash you!

00:19:50.080 --> 00:19:51.550
Y-Yuri!

00:19:53.350 --> 00:19:55.820
Run towards that scrap pile
500 meters ahead!

00:19:56.020 --> 00:19:59.750
I don't know what you're planning,
but pray that my legs don't give out first!

00:20:23.380 --> 00:20:26.350
H-Help me! Someone save me!

00:20:27.320 --> 00:20:28.580
That should be enough.

00:20:38.500 --> 00:20:39.570
Arthur!

00:20:39.570 --> 00:20:40.730
Melody!

00:20:41.340 --> 00:20:43.060
Papa! Mama!

00:20:43.370 --> 00:20:44.770
Papa!

00:20:44.970 --> 00:20:46.410
Mama!

00:20:57.720 --> 00:21:00.050
I wonder what kind of crime
Arthur will be charged with?

00:21:00.050 --> 00:21:01.360
I don't know.

00:21:01.360 --> 00:21:04.790
He's still a kid, but computer
crimes are a serious offense.

00:21:04.790 --> 00:21:10.490
Once the case report is submitted, he's
sure to be handed down a heavy punishment.

00:21:10.900 --> 00:21:13.960
We're the ones who should
be punished, aren't we?

00:21:16.600 --> 00:21:18.160
Hello!
Hello!

00:21:19.940 --> 00:21:22.910
Hi Eddie, how's your wound?

00:21:22.910 --> 00:21:24.610
Thanks, it's healing well.

00:21:24.610 --> 00:21:26.310
We're going to the beach now.

00:21:26.450 --> 00:21:29.440
We need to submit this case report
to headquarters, so could you sign it?

00:21:32.050 --> 00:21:35.990
Sorry, but could you also send the report to
3WA Headquarters once you're done signing it?

00:21:35.990 --> 00:21:39.080
We want to get to the beach
as soon as possible!

00:21:39.190 --> 00:21:40.460
See you!
See you!

00:21:40.460 --> 00:21:43.860
Good grief, those girls are like a typhoon.

00:21:43.860 --> 00:21:45.890
Darling, look!

00:21:46.100 --> 00:21:49.900
"The main culprits of the 463
hostage case are as follows:"

00:21:49.900 --> 00:21:55.780
"N. K. Crocker and T. Y. Stablos,
with no other accomplices."

00:21:55.780 --> 00:21:56.800
Huh?

00:21:57.510 --> 00:21:58.480
Those two...

00:21:58.480 --> 00:21:58.780
Mama!
Those two...

00:21:58.780 --> 00:21:59.580
Mama!

00:22:02.880 --> 00:22:04.850
Yay! Vacation, here we come!

00:22:04.850 --> 00:22:06.790
We're gonna party til we drop!

00:22:13.630 --> 00:22:15.290
All right!
All right!

00:22:43.320 --> 00:22:49.800
The mystery began after I fell asleep that time
Ano toki nemuri no ato ni okotta mistuerii

00:22:49.800 --> 00:22:56.300
I was guided by a voice from the future
Mirai kara kuru koe ni michibikareta no yo

00:22:56.300 --> 00:23:02.810
I passed through a distant, silvery time tunnel
Giniro haruka na taimu tonneru nukete

00:23:02.810 --> 00:23:09.410
And met a wanderer with unclouded eyes
Deatta sunda me no samayoibito

00:23:09.720 --> 00:23:11.850
Space Fantasy

00:23:11.850 --> 00:23:16.190
I came all this way just to meet you
Anata ni ai ni kokomade kita no

00:23:16.190 --> 00:23:18.330
Space Fantasy

00:23:18.330 --> 00:23:22.260
I came all this way just to meet you
Anata ni ai ni kokomade kita no

00:23:22.260 --> 00:23:28.740
Even if you were from another planet,
Tatoeba anata ga betsu no hoshi no hito demo

00:23:28.740 --> 00:23:34.970
It wouldn't matter to me, if I'd fallen in love
Watashi wa kamawanai aishita nara

00:23:35.810 --> 00:23:38.970
Dirty, Stormy Destiny

00:23:39.050 --> 00:23:41.720
Dirty, Stormy Destiny

00:23:41.720 --> 00:23:48.120
Love is zero G...
Koi wa mujuuryoku...

00:23:58.370 --> 00:24:01.370
Bye-bye. So long. Adieu. Arrivederci.

00:24:01.370 --> 00:24:03.500
Huh? W-W-What's that?

00:24:03.500 --> 00:24:06.540
I'm practicing how to say goodbye.
Why don't you practice, too?

00:24:06.540 --> 00:24:07.980
Saying goodbye?

00:24:07.980 --> 00:24:09.440
The end. Fin.

00:24:09.440 --> 00:24:11.450
And uh... Gah, this is such a pain!

00:24:11.450 --> 00:24:13.580
But what do you say when it's over?

00:24:13.580 --> 00:24:15.950
There's no need for words
when you're breaking up with a guy.

00:24:15.950 --> 00:24:18.220
Just smack him across the face
and that'll be the end of it.

00:24:18.220 --> 00:24:19.590
That doesn't seem right...

